# Deadweight — environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local`. Nothing here is required: the site is fully usable with
# this file absent, because every figure on it comes from the deterministic
# engine and the letter from the warehouse has an engine-written version that
# ships when no model is reachable.
#
# Server-side only unless the name starts with `NEXT_PUBLIC_`. Anything
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_` is compiled into the browser bundle — never put a key there.

# --- Google AI (the letter from the warehouse) -------------------------------
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Without it, `POST /api/letter` answers with the engine's own letter and says
# so (`source: "engine"`, `refused: "unavailable"`). With it, a model writes the
# prose and the route throws the draft away unless every number in it is one the
# engine inserted.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Comma-separated, tried in order, first survivor wins. Defaults to
# `gemini-3.8-flash,gemini-3.5-flash,gemini-2.5-flash`. Retiring an id is the
# failure mode these actually have, so it is config rather than a deploy.
# GEMINI_MODELS=gemini-3.8-flash,gemini-3.5-flash,gemini-2.5-flash

# --- Solana (the devnet notary) ---------------------------------------------
# Optional. Devnet only — this layer notarises a verdict and moves no value.
# Defaults to the public devnet endpoint, which is rate-limited but adequate.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC=https://api.devnet.solana.com
